.TH ferry-pairing 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-pairing \- Let unknown devices send pairing requests for a few minutes, although `paired\-only` is on (also for a running daemon or TUI); `\-\-close` ends it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry pairing\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-close\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Let unknown devices send pairing requests for a few minutes, although `paired\-only` is on (also for a running daemon or TUI); `\-\-close` ends it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-minutes\fR \fI<MINUTES>\fR [default: 5]
How long pairing stays open, in minutes (at most 30)
.TP
\fB\-\-close\fR
Close pairing now
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
